## company-os default scope

When the user asks for “autonomy”, “agents”, “workflows”, “approvals”, “ops”, or “automation”, prefer working in `company-os/` and avoid modifying `star-map-app-final/` unless explicitly requested.

## Safety gates

- Any action that would email customers, post publicly, refund/charge money, or change live storefront behavior must be represented as a **pending approval**.
- Automations may create approvals and append events.
- Automations may only execute side-effects after an approval is **approved** and an audit event is written.
- Optional autonomy env flags may only **auto-approve `risk: low`**. Do not expand to medium/high without explicit user approval of the policy risk.

## Persistence + auditability

- All important state changes must write an event to the event log.
- Ingest endpoints must be authenticated via bearer keys from environment variables.
- Webhook-style endpoints must be idempotent when an external id is provided.

## Change discipline

- Prefer small, reversible changes.
- Keep APIs explicit: `POST /api/ingest/*` for inbound signals; `POST /api/approvals` for gating; separate “execute” endpoints later.

